 "script": "Russia freed a seventy-four-year-old American on Wednesday, after more than four years. He's Stephen Hubbard, a former Michigan teacher, the Associated Press reports. Russia said he fought for Ukraine and sentenced him to nearly seven years. Here's how he got out. Trump says he asked Putin last week. The release came as envoy Steve Witkoff met Putin in Saint Petersburg. Trump says the US gave up no one in return. But one advocacy group says five other Americans it represents remain held. What should the US ask for next? Tell us below.",
